<v Daniel Alarcón>Yes. Melgar scores. People exploded, you know? Like you were cheering something that had actually happened. And the detail that he tells me that I'm always struck by is that when the lights came off and he went off stage, his uncle was crying, just weeping, with joy and with pride.
<v Daniel Alarcón>是的。梅尔加进球了。人们爆炸了，您知道吗？就像您在为一件实际发生的事情欢呼一样。让我总是深受触动的一个细节是，当灯光熄灭他走下舞台时，他的叔叔在哭，因喜悦和骄傲而哭泣。

